        "original_id": "26aeba3e-56e1-5a3b-9606-2ccdf8c58290",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giacomo Meyerbeer, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Roles: Opera composer, Composer\n- Concepts: Jewish birth, Classical era, Stage composition\n\nFacts:\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was born on 27 January 1756, was baptised as Johannes Chrysostomus Wolfgangus Theophilus Mozart, and became a prolific and influential composer of the Classical era.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer was born as Jacob Liebmann Beer on 5 September 1791 and was a German opera composer of Jewish birth.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart died on 5 December 1791.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer died on 2 May 1864 and has been described as perhaps the most successful stage composer of the nineteenth century.",
